Package: phdid
Title: Partial Homogeneity in Staggered Difference-in-Differences
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rohan", "Wagle", email = "rohan.wagle_ug2023@ashoka.edu.in",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Parush", "Arora",
           role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Estimation and specification testing for staggered
    difference-in-differences designs under partial homogeneity of the
    cohort-time average treatment effects (CATTs). Implements the Dirichlet
    Process mixture estimator ('Bayes-PH') via a collapsed Gibbs sampler,
    which marginalizes over the unknown partition of the cohort-time cells
    and reports co-clustering probabilities, and the 'l0'-penalized
    partial-homogeneity estimator ('l0-PH'), which arises as the
    fixed-variance maximum a posteriori partition under a pairwise
    partition prior. Also provides specification tests for whether the
    cohort-time effects carry recoverable heterogeneity at all, sampler
    diagnostics including exact partition enumeration for small designs,
    and a calibrated partial-homogeneity data-generating process. All
    estimators accept a vector of first-stage cohort-time effects together
    with their joint sampling covariance, so any heterogeneity-robust
    first-stage estimator may be used. Methods are described in Arora and
    Wagle (2026), "Partial Homogeneity in Staggered
    Difference-in-Differences".
